claude_worklog/agent_supervisor/tasks/claude_improve_expected_move_after_cost_coverage_from_shadow_false_blocks.json:43:  "prompt": "Task: Improve expected_move_after_cost coverage from shadow false-block evidence without loosening the strict V2 paper fill gate.\n\nHard constraints: Work only inside /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD. Do not modify /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT. Do not write old Redis. Do not place, cancel, or modify exchange orders. Do not change leverage or margin mode. Do not enable live. Do not create final approval or Redis trim approval tokens. Keep live_gate=blocked_human_only and live_symbols=[].\n\nCurrent evidence: paper_shadow_outcome_observer reports blocked intents that later beat estimated costs. These are model-review signals, not permission to trade from hindsight. V2 paper runtime now has strict gating, per-event trainer_source, feature_freshness_state, expected_move_after_cost fields, and a non-live paper position lifecycle. Positive paper edge remains unproven and legacy shutdown remains blocked.\n\nRequired work:\n1. Read current paper_shadow_outcome_observer status, decision improvement recommendations, paper edge recovery status, trainer bridge status, and paper event JSONL.\n2. Classify false blocks by reason, expected_move_source, confidence bucket, symbol, side, feature freshness, and whether expected_move_after_cost_bps was native, missing, or below threshold at decision time.\n3. Produce a model-improvement packet that identifies exactly which native expected_move_after_cost sources need improvement. Do not use future outcome labels to authorize current fills.\n4. If a safe code change is available, add only fail-closed reporting/scoring improvements that increase evidence coverage. Do not lower min_expected_move_after_cost_bps, do not lower confidence thresholds, and do not permit fills from historical false-block labels.\n5. Preserve no-trade correctness tracking and mark insufficient sample honestly.\n6. Update public/operator payloads with edge_status, false_block_count, no_trade_correct_count, allowed_paper_fill_count, sample status, live_gate, and live_symbols.\n7. Add tests proving future outcome labels cannot permit fills and the strict edge gate still blocks missing expected_move_after_cost, missing trainer_source, missing feature_freshness_state, low confidence, and symbols outside paper scope.\n8. Create Codex review marker codex_review_expected_move_after_cost_false_block_model_improvement.\n\nRequired outputs:\n- claude_worklog/final_readiness/paper_edge_recovery/latest/EXPECTED_MOVE_AFTER_COST_FALSE_BLOCK_MODEL_REVIEW.md\n- claude_worklog/final_readiness/paper_edge_recovery/latest/expected_move_after_cost_false_block_model_review.json\n- claude_worklog/final_readiness/paper_edge_recovery/latest/operator_dashboard_payload.json\n- v2/frontend/public/paper_edge_recovery/latest/operator_dashboard_payload.json\n\nGO/NO-GO classification must be one of:\n- EXPECTED_MOVE_AFTER_COST_MODEL_REVIEW_READY_EDGE_PENDING\n- EXPECTED_MOVE_AFTER_COST_MODEL_REVIEW_BLOCKED_INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\n- EXPECTED_MOVE_AFTER_COST_MODEL_REVIEW_BLOCKED_SAFETY_REGRESSION\n\nValidation required: py_compile, targeted tests, JSON validation, secret scan, forbidden mutation scan. Do not claim live-ready, canary-ready, positive edge, or legacy shutdown readiness.",
